  "notes": "{燃|も}やす is a transitive godan verb meaning to burn something deliberately.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {燃|も}える (intransitive, to burn by itself)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ゴミを{燃|も}やす: to burn garbage\n- {落|お}ち{葉|ば}を{燃|も}やす: to burn fallen leaves\n- {書類|しょるい}を{燃|も}やす: to burn documents\n\nGARBAGE SORTING:\n- {燃|も}えるゴミ/{可燃|かねん}ゴミ: combustible garbage\n- {燃|も}えないゴミ/{不燃|ふねん}ゴミ: non-combustible garbage\n\nFIGURATIVE USE:\n- {情熱|じょうねつ}を{燃|も}やす: to burn with passion\n- {闘志|とうし}を{燃|も}やす: to be fired up (for competition)\n\nRELATED:\n- {燃|も}える: to burn (intransitive)\n- {焼|や}く: to grill, roast, bake",
